      "writtenOn": "2026-08-24T12:50:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "infra.shell() never raises — it catches CalledProcessError and returns (rc, stdout) — and the result is discarded here, so a failed cp leaves /tmp/schema empty. The connector then downloads the models from the device, the mount succeeds and the flow passes, so the suite silently becomes a second copy of test_clustering_crud. Could we assert rc \u003d\u003d 0 and that the seeded file exists?",
      "revId": "ebccbc89ffc35e59168ed70887944fc98647aeee",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
    },
