      "side": 1,
      "message": "mkdir -p succeeds whether or not the directory already existed, so this rm -rf can delete a pre-existing /tmp/schema and everything in it — and /tmp/schema is also the repo-wide default for schema_directory (netconf.py Line 147), so it is not a name this suite owns. Two framework runs on one machine would also collide. Could the suite use a run-unique directory(maybe under pytest\u0027s tmp_path, or containing the process ID in the name, etc...). Then we know we\u0027re removing only what we created during the test.",
